irection-only`:\n  - Conversion is one option among several, and parents choose it, not the board.\n  - The annex says a law that lists conversion as one option among several is direction-only. It does not match rung 5 (\"Convert failing district schools into charters run by independent operators\").\n  - It says nothing about how readily a board should authorize new charters.\n- **Why `no-evidence` rather than `direction-only`:** the education page speaks of him in the third person (\"Steve Hilton will…\"). Under V1's \"voice decides, not domain\" rule, that makes it a third-party description of a promise, so it cannot support a chair. A coder who instead reads the page as Hilton's own words would reach BLANK `direction-only`, so the coders may split on the blank reason.\n- **Other two pages:** I coded both as `off`. The \"New California Dream Charters\" are development charters for new cities, not schools. The street-vending page only mentions charter cities.\n- **`needs_source`:** Hilton's own first-person words on authorizing charter schools or converting failing schools to charters.\n- **Quote:** I included the parent-trigger sentence and coded it `lever` / `lever-named`, quotable.","ttft_ms":16491,"type":"result","duration_ms":38130,"uuid":"8ee688a7-5db6-466c-a0f7-e8caf8baf64a","ttft_stream_ms":4569,"time_to_request_ms":90,"first_content_frame_ms":4570,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
